and an Olympian on our team.

01:09:08.580 --> 01:09:09.436
If we don't win-

01:09:09.436 --> 01:09:10.333
It's a problem.

01:09:10.333 --> 01:09:11.166
It's a problem.

01:09:11.166 --> 01:09:12.000
And we did, we won.

01:09:12.000 --> 01:09:12.833
It's a problem.

01:09:12.833 --> 01:09:13.983
Team yellow won the whole thing.

01:09:13.983 --> 01:09:16.710
But just to aspect of,

01:09:16.710 --> 01:09:19.352
I mean, between all the goofing off it,

01:09:19.352 --> 01:09:20.550
like you're saying,

01:09:20.550 --> 01:09:25.550
it was nice to have
conversations with people

01:09:27.018 --> 01:09:31.560
where they valued our experience
and we were fascinated

01:09:31.560 --> 01:09:34.170
with theirs and how
there's so much overlap

01:09:34.170 --> 01:09:36.510
in where they're going and
what they're trying to build

01:09:36.510 --> 01:09:40.530
and what we've already
built in a lot of ways

01:09:40.530 --> 01:09:43.620
and just how we can kinda pay
it forward and help em out.

01:09:43.620 --> 01:09:46.830
But also there's so much for
us to learn at the same time

01:09:46.830 --> 01:09:49.192
because like the emphasis on shorts

01:09:49.192 --> 01:09:52.950
is a totally new thing for YouTube.

01:09:52.950 --> 01:09:55.200
Like grappling with the TikTok of it all.

01:09:55.200 --> 01:09:59.730
And so everyone there has this spirit of

01:09:59.730 --> 01:10:03.780
taking these tools and
what the algorithms,

01:10:03.780 --> 01:10:04.860
how they behave,

01:10:04.860 --> 01:10:09.270
being a student of
finding the intersection

01:10:09.270 --> 01:10:12.300
between technology and self-expression

01:10:12.300 --> 01:10:14.820
to reach an audience
and connect with them.

01:10:14.820 --> 01:10:17.760
And I just found that very invigorating.

01:10:17.760 --> 01:10:22.760
You know, it was cool to be
seen as people who were OGs

01:10:25.290 --> 01:10:28.230
still relevant and valuable
to their experience.

01:10:28.230 --> 01:10:33.230
I mean, Stevie was invited to
be one of the speakers there

01:10:33.420 --> 01:10:34.470
talking about,

01:10:34.470 --> 01:10:36.570
there were like four breakout
sessions that everybody could

01:10:36.570 --> 01:10:38.133
go to and they happened twice.

01:10:38.975 --> 01:10:40.500
So they ended up being like small groups.

01:10:40.500 --> 01:10:43.800
So she came to Palm Springs
to talk about building a team,

01:10:43.800 --> 01:10:47.190
which a lot of YouTubers
are interested in doing.

01:10:47.190 --> 01:10:48.960
And it's a hard thing to figure out.

01:10:48.960 --> 01:10:50.520
We weren't allowed to see her though.

01:10:50.520 --> 01:10:51.353
I did see her.

01:10:51.353 --> 01:10:53.130
How did you see her?

01:10:53.130 --> 01:10:55.491
I walked up to her before her thing

01:10:55.491 --> 01:10:57.750
and she immediately started laughing

01:10:57.750 --> 01:11:01.530
because I was wearing
my glasses and my shorts

01:11:01.530 --> 01:11:03.030
and my Palm Springs shirt.

01:11:03.030 --> 01:11:05.940
And she was like, you really
look Palm Springs right now.

01:11:05.940 --> 01:11:09.390
It's like, well, I'm having a ball.

01:11:09.390 --> 01:11:11.334
And she was like, well
you gotta get outta here.

01:11:11.334 --> 01:11:14.610
But I'm proud of what we have at Mythical

01:11:14.610 --> 01:11:16.110
that it's not just about the two of us,

01:11:16.110 --> 01:11:17.070
it's about our team.

01:11:17.070 --> 01:11:20.250
And like Stevie represented him
being there and like lots of

01:11:20.250 --> 01:11:22.440
people like even people who've been around

01:11:22.440 --> 01:11:24.171
the block many times like Marquez saying,

01:11:24.171 --> 01:11:29.171
he got a lot out of her session.

01:11:30.660 --> 01:11:32.070
It's really cool.

01:11:32.070 --> 01:11:35.370
And then they had this thing
called a magic mirror where you

01:11:35.370 --> 01:11:37.881
could go up to it like a
mirror, mirror on the wall.

01:11:37.881 --> 01:11:39.990
You ask em something about YouTube

01:11:39.990 --> 01:11:41.820
and then you get a response.

01:11:41.820 --> 01:11:43.260
And I don't know exactly how it worked,

01:11:43.260 --> 01:11:48.240
but we were supposed to go in
and answer people's questions,

01:11:48.240 --> 01:11:50.490
but we interacted with the mirror.

01:11:50.490 --> 01:11:51.600
There was a guy,

01:11:51.600 --> 01:11:52.620
I don't know if you knew this Rhett,

01:11:52.620 --> 01:11:54.180
but there was a guy behind the mirror.

01:11:54.180 --> 01:11:55.880
He was speaking through a speaker,

01:11:57.055 --> 01:11:57.888
so it looked like the mirror was talking.

01:11:57.888 --> 01:11:58.800
I know which guy it was too.

01:11:58.800 --> 01:12:02.400
And then when we came out after
interacting with this guy,

01:12:02.400 --> 01:12:05.160
like the YouTube person
was like, how did it go?

01:12:05.160 --> 01:12:09.060
And I was like, honestly,
he was kind of an asshole.

01:12:09.060 --> 01:12:14.060
And then you said, well
like he's a mirror.

01:12:14.220 --> 01:12:17.910
He's just reflecting back
what he gets from you.

01:12:17.910 --> 01:12:19.860
And I was like, oh, okay.

01:12:19.860 --> 01:12:21.360
That's pretty fair.

01:12:22.590 --> 01:12:24.720
So but he was a fan,

01:12:24.720 --> 01:12:26.250
